From: kylechar <kylechar@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:45:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] Flush after failed write pixels

Original change's description:
> Flush after failed write pixels
>
> If RasterImplementation WritePixels() encounters a failure in
> SkCanvas::writePixels() ensure it still flushes and submits all pending
> work. The discard clear operation, if write pixels is overwriting the
> whole texture, is already recorded on the SkSurface which can cause a
> future write access to the same shared image to fail to clear it.
>
> There is similar logic CopyPixelsToTexture() which already
> unconditionally flushed+submitted but didn't check if writePixels()
> failed. Fix this as well.
>
> Lastly change surface->wait() calls in both places to just ignore the
> return value. The wait() call can fail if GrContext is abandoned but in
> that case it just doesn't matter. The writePixel() operation that
> happens afterwards will fail for the same reason.
>
